{"title":"EU fact of the day","link":"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/954705365/0/marginalrevolution~EU-fact-of-the-day.html","date":1777359079000,"content":"<p>You do not hear this point made too often, yet it is true:</p>\r\n<blockquote><p><span>Very interesting new study finding that *even in large European cities*, in most places it is easier to access opportunities by car than by public transport </span><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://t.co/YzQbrtfR0i\" target=\"_blank\"><span>https://</span>arxiv.org/pdf/2604.01019</a><span> The exceptions are Paris, Zurich and the innermost parts of Milan and Barcelona</span></p></blockquote>\r\n<p>That is <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://x.com/aboutJoy/status/2048754764364571082\" target=\"_blank\">from Giulio Mattioli</a>, citing the paper by Bruno Campenelli, et.al.  In turn via <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://x.com/aboutJoy\" target=\"_blank\">Joy Buchanan</a>.</p>\r\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/04/eu-fact-of-the-day.html\">EU fact of the day</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com\">Marginal REVOLUTION</a>.</p>\r\n<img height=\"1\" width=\"1\" src=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/i/954705365/0/marginalrevolution\" />\r\n<div><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/28/954705365/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/fblike20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/29/954705365/marginalrevolution,\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/pinterest20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/24/954705365/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/x.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/19/954705365/